ID: Ch9-Intervention
TEXT:

 "Oh yeah? And who's going to lead us to the ogre stronghold with the girl gone?"

"We have the bearing," Daren says, his jaw set like stone. "We're close enough to reach the walls without an escort. Step aside, Barry."

I draw my dagger with a short laugh. "Not happening."

"Whoa-ho-ho, hold on, lads!" Hadrik steps in, planting himself between us with broad palms out. "Take a breath before steel bites bone. Do you want the ballads to remember us as the warriors who took the Magium tournament by storm, or the fools who butchered each other in a pasture before the opening bell?"

"Daren, please," Rose says softly, stepping up beside him. "Put it away."

Daren glances from Hadrik to Rose, then down at my blade. He lets out a slow, heavy breath and slides the broadsword back into its scabbard.

"I won't fight you, Barry," he says quietly. "I hoped to make you see reason, but if a dragon couldn't move you, a sword won't either. You were right about Kate. I can only pray your instincts hold up twice."

Daren and Hadrik take their stations at the crest without another word. Rose, Illuna, and I head down the slope in silence.

At the entrance of Flower's tent, Illuna pauses with her hand on the canvas.

"Your intervention was pointless, human," she says over her shoulder. "I could have dismantled that healer in seconds."

"Don't be modest," I say. "Friends back each other up."

"You labor under the delusion that we are friends. You couldn't be further from the truth."

choice(""Relax, I only wanted to make sure we don't lose our only guide."", Ch9-Guide, v_current_scene = Ch9-Guide)
choice(""I didn't do this for you, I did it for Flower's sake."", Ch9-Sake, v_current_scene = Ch9-Sake)
choice(""If I wanted you dead I'd have let Daren finish the argument."", Ch9-Love, v_current_scene = Ch9-Love)


ID: Ch9-Guide
TEXT:

 "Relax, I only wanted to make sure we don't lose our only guide. It wasn't anything personal."

"Pragmatic," Illuna says. "Self-interest I can respect. But heed this: do not mistake me for an ally. This arrangement dissolves the moment those collars drop. Expect nothing more."

She slips inside and laces the flap shut.

"Good night, Illuna!" Rose calls out cheerfully. No answer comes from within.

Rose turns to me, smiling in the moonlight. "I'd say that went remarkably well."

"You think?"

"Of course! Did you see how her posture eased when you stepped in? Underneath the thorns, she isn't so different from the rest of us."

"I'm starting to hear Flower talking through you."

"There's a bit of Flower in all of us, Barry," Rose says, tapping my chest. "Yours is just buried under five layers of cynicism and dry remarks."

choice("Continue", Ch9-Backpack, v_current_scene = Ch9-Backpack)


ID: Ch9-Sake
TEXT:

 "I didn't do this for you, I did it for Flower's sake."

"Your sentiment for the child is irrelevant," Illuna says, "though it explains your interference. But heed this: do not mistake me for an ally. This arrangement dissolves the moment those collars drop. Expect nothing more."

She slips inside and laces the flap shut.

"Good night, Illuna!" Rose calls out cheerfully. No answer comes from within.

Rose turns to me, smiling in the moonlight. "I'd say that went remarkably well."

"You think?"

"Of course! Did you see how her posture eased when you stepped in? Underneath the thorns, she isn't so different from the rest of us."

"I'm starting to hear Flower talking through you."

"There's a bit of Flower in all of us, Barry," Rose says, tapping my chest. "Yours is just buried under five layers of cynicism and dry remarks."

