achievement("Keen observer",v_ac_ch9_observer)
#if(v_ch9_take_rose == 0 && v_hearing < 2) {
 

We leave Kate and Rose concealed in the thicket and step out toward the stronghold.

Ten minutes through the thinning brush brings us to the edge of the cleared perimeter. A wasteland of stumps and scorched earth stretches for a mile in every direction, leading up to a rocky prominence. The fort crowns the hill—a sprawling stone fortress spanning some four hundred thousand square feet, its thirty-foot granite curtain walls unbroken save for a massive timber gate that stands wide open.

Through the gate, the inner courtyard is deserted. No cookfires, no patrols, no movement along the ramparts.

"They aren't bothering to disguise the ambush, are they?" Hadrik mutters, cracking his knuckles as we cross the threshold into the yard.

"Eyes sharp," Daren says, broadsword resting across his forearm. "They could strike from any angle."

As we advance past the gatehouse, a frantic, muffled rattling breaks out from Flower's chest.

"Stop it!" Flower snaps at the locket. "The second I unlatch you, you'll shriek and give away our position to the whole fort. I'm not falling for that again."

The amulet thrashes against her tunic, the muffled squeals growing sharper.

}
#if(v_ch9_take_rose == 1 && v_hearing < 2) {
 

We ready our weapons and step out toward the stronghold.

Ten minutes through the thinning brush brings us to the edge of the cleared perimeter. A wasteland of stumps and scorched earth stretches for a mile in every direction, leading up to a rocky prominence. The fort crowns the hill—a sprawling stone fortress spanning some four hundred thousand square feet, its thirty-foot granite curtain walls unbroken save for a massive timber gate that stands wide open.

Through the gate, the inner courtyard is deserted. No cookfires, no patrols, no movement along the ramparts.

"They aren't bothering to disguise the ambush, are they?" Hadrik mutters, cracking his knuckles as we cross the threshold into the yard.

"Eyes sharp," Daren says, broadsword resting across his forearm. "They could strike from any angle."

As we advance past the gatehouse, a frantic, muffled rattling breaks out from Flower's chest.

"Stop it!" Flower snaps at the locket. "The second I unlatch you, you'll shriek and give away our position to the whole fort. I'm not falling for that again."

The amulet thrashes against her tunic, the muffled squeals growing sharper.

}
#if(v_ch9_take_rose == 0 && v_perception == 0 && v_hearing >= 2) {
 

While Flower and Kate finish speaking, the faint snap of a twig catches my ear behind us. I pivot, dagger drawn, scanning the brush. Nothing moves. The leaves hang dead still.

I hold my breath, listening, but the woods remain silent. Tension playing tricks on my nerves.

I shake it off and sheath the blade. We leave Kate and Rose concealed in the ferns, and begin the final approach to the stronghold.

}
#if(v_ch9_take_rose == 1 && v_perception == 0 && v_hearing >= 2) {
 

While Flower and Kate finish speaking, the faint snap of a twig catches my ear behind us. I pivot, dagger drawn, scanning the brush. Nothing moves. The leaves hang dead still.

I hold my breath, listening, but the woods remain silent. Tension playing tricks on my nerves.

I shake it off, ready my crossbow, and we begin the final approach to the stronghold.

}
#if(v_hearing >= 2 && v_perception >= 1) {
 

While Flower and Kate finish speaking, the faint snap of a twig catches my ear behind us. I pivot instantly, eyes sweeping the undergrowth.

At first glance, the thicket looks undisturbed. Then I spot it—a patch of tall dry grass five yards out is compressed flat against the soil, bending under invisible weight.

I raise my crossbow, aligning the sights two feet above the flattened stems.

"Barry, what are you doing?" Daren asks. "Lower the bow and let's move."

I squeeze the trigger.

The bolt snaps forward and jerks to a dead halt in midair. A dark bead of blood wells against the iron tip. The air shimmers like heat off an anvil, and an eight-foot brute fades into view with my bolt sunk deep into his gut. Leathery gray skin, narrow brow, yellowed lower tusks jutting past a heavy snout—staring down at his bleeding belly with utter bewilderment.

}
