ID: Ch9-Nice
TEXT:

#if(v_ch9_take_rose == 0) {
 The wounded ogre bellows, ripping the bolt from his flesh with one hand while hoisting a five-foot oak club with the other. A second brute shimmers into view beside him, weapon already swinging.

They don't get the chance.

In a clean blur of steel, Daren's broadsword shears through the first ogre's throat, while Hadrik launches off the turf, driving a heavy boot into the second brute's skull with a sickening crunch. Both bodies crash into the loam like felled timber.

"Sharp shooting, Barry," Daren says, flicking dark blood from his blade. "Invisibility weaves... their shaman is far more dangerous than we anticipated."

"We can't leave Rose and Kate exposed out here with invisible patrols in the brush," I say.

"Agreed," Daren says, turning to the women. "You're coming inside with us. No arguments."

We verify the perimeter is clear, check our weapons, and begin the march toward the fort.

}
#if(v_ch9_take_rose == 1) {
 The wounded ogre bellows, ripping the bolt from his flesh with one hand while hoisting a five-foot oak club with the other. A second brute shimmers into view beside him, weapon already swinging.

